--delimiter <char> (field delimiter, default ',', --delimiter=<char> accepted);
--select <cols> (filter and reorder output columns by header name,
comma-separated list, unknown names are an error);
--types (infer JSON numbers from integers/decimals and booleans from
bare true/false, everything else stays a string);
--stats (report data row count and per-column empty counts,
composes with --select).

Summary point — all options compose freely; usage:
node src/cli.ts [--delimiter <char>] [--select <cols>] [--types] [--stats] <file.csv>" && git log --oneline -1 && git rev-parse HEAD

